edges are not, and "},{"code":"{u, v}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same edge as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"{v, u}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot (none while the vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order, each its own slot). Edges are kept in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, so an edge’s position in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each slot has a row of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the slots of its neighbors and a parallel row of the positions of its incident edges; each edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is in both its endpoints’ rows, and a self-loop twice in its vertex’s row (as Boost stores it).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The rows share one array per kind, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"many vertices it has. A hash table from unordered slot pair to position (open addressing with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"multiplicative hash, not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Dictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s SipHash) answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in O(1) expected.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each edge keeps the orientation it was first inserted with."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://AdjacencyListModule/documentation/AdjacencyListModule/UndirectedAdjacencyList/Hashable-Implementations":{"title":"Hashable Implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/Hashable-Implementations","abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/undirectedadjacencylist\/hashable-implementations"},"doc://AdjacencyListModule/documentation/AdjacencyListModule/UndirectedAdjacencyList/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"removeAllEdges"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"keepingCapacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/undirectedadjacencylist\/removealledges(keepingcapacity:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Removes every edge, keeping every vertex.","type":"text"}],"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"title":"removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)"},"doc://AdjacencyListModule/documentation/AdjacencyListModu